@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Trade reserve evidence — build 2228
+
+## Scope and source identity
+
+Start from production v1.22.12/build 2227, commit 40226bb497a5b5c30047cc5f98e49c4008c67992, tree de2827e28dea58e7174c938ba4b38930e0892bea. Public readiness and origin/main agreed at investigation start. No production Trade search, synchronization, preference update, ranking change or lineup submission was performed.
+
+The supplied Granite build 2226 observation reports 128 assessed packages and zero qualified recommendations. Its complete matched per-package source diagnostics were not located in retained local evidence. Consequently, this work does not attribute counts or specific upstream causes to those 128 packages, reconstruct the historical run from current rosters, or claim a live qualified offer. Zero recommendations is not a defect.
+
+## Reproductions and confirmed causes
+
+1. A disposable twelve-team one-QB publication with QB/RB/WR/TE/FLEX/K/DEF gives the owner's reserves a verified 10-point disjoint subtotal and an active bench receiver without a numerical projection. Before and after full reserve effects remain unknown. The partner independently has supported 10-point pre-trade and 20-point post-trade reserve production. The old primary summary reduced both franchises to a generic incomplete-depth warning when later weeks lacked coverage. Individual reserve rows were already retained; the defect was failure to explain their distinct support and boundaries in the visible decision.
+2. In a Superflex control with no K/DEF slots, the remaining rostered K/DEF players were counted as usable reserve candidates despite having no legal slot. The optimizer correctly selected none, but the nonempty candidate count prevented an established empty usable pool from becoming numerical zero. Missing projections for those provably irrelevant positions could also poison reserve coverage. This is a shared reserve-population boundary issue, not a missing Sleeper forecast or a Market-price problem.
+
+## Narrow corrections
+
+Canonical reserve preparation uses the existing fantasy-position and league-slot eligibility rules to exclude only players proven unable to fill any configured slot. Unknown eligibility remains unresolved. Required Granite K/DEF projections remain necessary. A supported, genuinely empty usable replacement population is zero; an unprojected eligible player is unknown. The prepared-profile methodology identity advances to v5 so old and corrected profiles are not silently combined. Starting-lineup optimization, scoring coefficients and submitted starters are unchanged.
+
+Presentation admits each side/week/phase against the pinned league, season, scoring, generation, owner, slot, player projection and subtotal. Reserve-specific snapshot identity is checked independently. Known partial subtotals, covered slots, eligible candidate counts and missing-player explanations remain distinct from full reserve production. A subtotal does not become a delta, bound or second starting lineup. The primary card shows the first requested weekly reserve context; all other retained weeks remain independently available in the existing lineup disclosure. Source freshness is requalified with the existing rule at render time.
+
+A missing projection is described as missing from the prepared compatible publication; this does not establish upstream Sleeper absence. Unknown identity uses a safe fallback. Out/IR, byes, unsupported positions, future-week participation and unavailable starters retain their actual evidence qualifications. A defect in one phase cannot erase a valid partner/other-week comparison.
+
+## Source-to-screen chain and controls
+
+Sleeper-shaped fixture feed -> ProjectionService scoring/identity publication -> pinned prepare_team_strength profile -> evaluate_horizon_impact independently optimized pre/post legal rosters -> package_quality unchanged -> bound completed lineup details -> shared reserve presentation -> Trade primary summaries and expandable slot tables.
+
+Controls include one-QB/K/DEF, Superflex without dedicated TE, known zero, missing eligible projections, missing irrelevant K/DEF projections, unknown eligibility, missing starter, wrong owner/generation/scoring/snapshot, different week projections, aging, partial horizon, source-free rendering, and an actual fixture-qualified +8 consolidation with a -1 reserve cost under all three strategies. Existing extreme-overpay, Custom partial valuation, exact-pick, admission, cancellation and cleanup suites remain mandatory.
+
+No customer-facing beta/prerelease wording was found in production rendering sources. The four-size Trade browser control asserts its absence; open registration, welcome demos and legitimate disclaimers are unchanged.
+
+## Validation and remaining limits
+
+Original failed attempts are retained separately: initial probe import setup; Superflex assertion exposing the canonical issue; browser assertion expecting unnecessary trailing zeros; consequent missing screenshot-directory artifact. None counts as passing evidence. Clean exact-candidate canonical/hosted results and readable original consoles are published separately with source and checksums.
+
+Fixtures demonstrate compatible source-to-screen behavior, not live Granite recovery or a historically qualified offer. The 128-case historical cause denominator remains unavailable. Fixture cleanup is not a proof of indefinite leak freedom. Desktop Chromium and touch emulation do not establish physical iPhone/Safari acceptance.
+
+## Independent Scout acceptance
+
+1. Verify release identity and current safe resource admission without starting discovery automatically.
+2. On a permitted retained or newly authorized assessment, inspect both teams' primary reserve summary and expanded before/after lineups. Verify exact week/scoring/publication identity, K/DEF/FLEX assignments and point sums.
+3. Confirm a partial subtotal is labeled partial and its missing player/phase is explained; an independently valid partner/week remains visible.
+4. Confirm a zero appears only for a supported zero or proven empty usable pool, and submitted Sleeper starters remain separate.
+5. Confirm verdict, Neutral/Custom mode, exact picks and workspace remain unchanged. Any new live heavy search requires contemporaneously safe admission and separate bounded acceptance planning.
